WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.340
A laptop provides portability, while a desktop offers easier expansion and larger displays.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.369
A mini PC can serve as a compact dedicated station.

00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:22.082
A virtual machine can separate research software and files from the host, but it still depends on host security, storage, and disciplined configuration.

00:00:22.082 --> 00:00:27.111
Windows, Linux, and macOS can all support responsible OSINT work.

00:00:27.111 --> 00:00:34.326
The best choice is the platform the organization can secure, patch, back up, and support.

00:00:34.326 --> 00:00:39.354
Specialized appearance or unfamiliar complexity does not create better intelligence.

00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:47.881
Memory requirements depend on browser tabs, local document processing, mapping, spreadsheets, virtual machines, and approved local AI tools.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:52.035
Sufficient memory prevents constant swapping and unstable multitasking.

00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:58.813
Storage should use dependable solid-state media with capacity for active cases and recovery operations.

00:00:58.813 --> 00:01:07.340
A second display can improve note taking and source comparison, but screen privacy and physical workspace design matter.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:14.554
Portable systems may need privacy filters or careful placement when sensitive case material is visible.

00:01:14.554 --> 00:01:20.020
Virtual machines are useful for snapshots, reproducible environments, and tool separation.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.612
Snapshots are not backups, and isolation is not absolute.

00:01:24.612 --> 00:01:34.450
Keep the host, hypervisor, guest system, and browsers updated, and understand where copied files, shared folders, and clipboard data are stored.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.418
Select practical reliability.

00:01:36.418 --> 00:01:41.884
Use supported hardware, tested encryption, known recovery methods, and documented peripherals.

00:01:41.884 --> 00:01:49.099
Build enough headroom for normal workloads without buying complexity that cannot be maintained or audited.
